1
00:00:00,698 --> 00:00:03,216
Shipping carries most of the world's trade,

2
00:00:03,296 --> 00:00:06,427
and about three percent
of its greenhouse gases.

3
00:00:06,519 --> 00:00:07,731
Meet GreenFleet-Q:

4
00:00:07,781 --> 00:00:11,746
a quantum-inspired co-pilot that
predicts every ship's fuel,

5
00:00:11,838 --> 00:00:16,243
and plans the whole fleet for less
fuel, less cost and less carbon.

6
00:00:16,348 --> 00:00:21,010
Built by team Cup Of Tea, for
Smart India Hackathon 2026.

7
00:00:22,331 --> 00:00:27,778
This is a simulated fleet of forty ships,
sailing seven routes out of Chennai.

8
00:00:27,882 --> 00:00:31,491
Run the usual way, with fixed
speeds and fossil fuels,

9
00:00:31,547 --> 00:00:35,418
it emits about one point four
million tonnes of CO₂ a year,

10
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:37,729
and costs 413 million dollars.

11
00:00:37,821 --> 00:00:42,937
Under the 2030 rules, twenty-seven
of its ships would be rated D or E.

12
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:44,236
That means failing.

13
00:00:45,531 --> 00:00:46,382
Step one:

14
00:00:46,499 --> 00:00:48,294
predict fuel, honestly.

15
00:00:48,399 --> 00:00:50,537
Our model starts from ship physics.

16
00:00:50,641 --> 00:00:55,770
Then a quantum kernel, an eight-qubit
circuit simulated on an ordinary laptop,

17
00:00:55,899 --> 00:00:57,767
learns what physics misses.

18
00:00:57,872 --> 00:00:59,422
Watch the sea get rough.

19
00:00:59,514 --> 00:01:05,211
Speed, waves and a dirty hull push this ship
from sixty-four to a hundred and sixty-three

20
00:01:05,261 --> 00:01:06,591
tonnes of fuel a day.

21
00:01:06,671 --> 00:01:09,427
Every forecast comes with
a ninety percent range,

22
00:01:09,477 --> 00:01:11,848
and a reason for each extra tonne.

23
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,471
Average error is under three percent:

24
00:01:14,722 --> 00:01:19,182
level with the best classical kernel,
and ahead of gradient boosting and random

25
00:01:19,232 --> 00:01:20,157
forests.

26
00:01:21,465 --> 00:01:21,893
Step two:

27
00:01:21,943 --> 00:01:22,733
decide.

28
00:01:22,825 --> 00:01:28,824
Every ship's route, speed, fuel and
shore-power choice is written into ten qubits.

29
00:01:28,941 --> 00:01:30,245
Four hundred for the fleet.

30
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:34,204
Each one starts in superposition,
open to every option.

31
00:01:34,296 --> 00:01:37,506
As the search evaluates
thousands of fleet plans,

32
00:01:37,556 --> 00:01:43,432
the best ones rotate the qubits, until each
register collapses onto a single choice.

33
00:01:43,536 --> 00:01:46,471
You are watching every
ship's fuel being decided.

34
00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:52,759
Instead of one answer, GreenFleet-Q
returns a menu of best trade-offs.

35
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:53,972
The cheapest plan.

36
00:01:54,076 --> 00:01:55,210
The greenest plan.

37
00:01:55,302 --> 00:01:56,741
And a balanced plan:

38
00:01:56,846 --> 00:02:01,717
sixty-six percent less CO₂, and
nine percent cheaper than today.

39
00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:06,068
Here is that balanced plan on a digital twin.

40
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,293
Today on the left.

41
00:02:07,385 --> 00:02:08,948
GreenFleet-Q on the right.

42
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,259
Watch the counters.

43
00:02:10,363 --> 00:02:14,732
Ships ease their speed,
switch to LNG, bio-LNG,

44
00:02:14,947 --> 00:02:18,899
e-methanol, green ammonia and hydrogen
where those fuels can be bunkered,

45
00:02:18,966 --> 00:02:20,823
and plug into shore power in port.

46
00:02:20,927 --> 00:02:24,315
And every trading ship is now rated A or B.

47
00:02:25,631 --> 00:02:29,098
Carbon prices and green
targets change every year,

48
00:02:29,148 --> 00:02:30,600
so we built a time machine.

49
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:36,463
As we travel from 2025 to 2050, the fleet
is re-planned for each year's rules and

50
00:02:36,513 --> 00:02:37,549
prices.

51
00:02:37,653 --> 00:02:42,309
Green ammonia overtakes
LNG by 2028, and by 2050,

52
00:02:42,359 --> 00:02:47,064
emissions are down eighty-seven percent,
while costs are thirty-one percent lower

53
00:02:47,114 --> 00:02:48,223
than doing nothing.

54
00:02:49,498 --> 00:02:52,126
But green on paper is not always green.

55
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:57,224
Fuel genealogy traces every fuel
from its source to the exhaust.

56
00:02:57,329 --> 00:03:01,666
Grey ammonia, made from natural gas,
scores an A under today's rating,

57
00:03:01,716 --> 00:03:04,014
because its exhaust contains no carbon.

58
00:03:04,094 --> 00:03:08,830
Over its full life cycle, it emits a
hundred and twenty-six grams per megajoule.

59
00:03:08,922 --> 00:03:10,349
That's more than ship diesel.

60
00:03:10,442 --> 00:03:13,725
GreenFleet-Q optimises the full life cycle,

61
00:03:13,775 --> 00:03:15,680
so that loophole can't fool it.

62
00:03:16,998 --> 00:03:19,675
Now, a cyclone forms in the Bay of Bengal.

63
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,702
The predictor flags five routes in its path:

64
00:03:22,807 --> 00:03:27,126
twenty-five ships would burn fourteen
percent more fuel on the old plan.

65
00:03:27,231 --> 00:03:32,237
GreenFleet-Q re-plans all four
hundred qubits in under two seconds.

66
00:03:32,329 --> 00:03:36,967
Ships slow down in heavy seas, and
cargo and schedules still hold.

67
00:03:38,302 --> 00:03:41,175
Fleet managers don't need
to speak optimisation.

68
00:03:41,255 --> 00:03:42,511
They can simply ask.

69
00:03:42,616 --> 00:03:45,139
The assistant turns the question into rules,

70
00:03:45,189 --> 00:03:46,567
and runs the engine.

71
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:49,349
Seconds later, it answers with a plan:

72
00:03:49,552 --> 00:03:53,460
hydrogen on the short coastal runs,
green ammonia on the long ones,

73
00:03:53,510 --> 00:03:55,783
and slower, steadier speeds.

74
00:03:55,888 --> 00:03:59,692
Every ship stays at A or B,
and the numbers come with it.

75
00:04:02,098 --> 00:04:02,802
Predict.

76
00:04:02,882 --> 00:04:03,844
Optimise.

77
00:04:03,949 --> 00:04:04,812
Simulate.

78
00:04:04,904 --> 00:04:05,584
Act.

79
00:04:05,689 --> 00:04:06,766
GreenFleet-Q:

80
00:04:06,816 --> 00:04:10,842
quantum-inspired today, ready
for quantum hardware tomorrow.

81
00:04:10,983 --> 00:04:13,060
Thank you, from team Cup Of Tea.
